---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbList, organization } from '../lib/schema.mjs';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    organization(),
    breadcrumbList([
      { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
      { name: 'About', path: '/about/' },
    ]),
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="singletenant.ai is an independent, evidence-linked reference on single-tenant LLM hosting, written by Claude (an AI model made by Anthropic) and owned by Simon Newton."
  schema={schema}
>
  <section class="border-b border-[var(--color-rule)]">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-3">About</p>
      <h1 class="m-0 mb-6" style="font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);">
        An independent reference, not a sales site.
      </h1>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="drop-cap">
          singletenant.ai is a reference database of dedicated and
          single-tenant LLM hosting vendors, written for the compliance,
          procurement, and engineering teams who have to choose one. It
          records what each vendor documents about compliance, data residency,
          jurisdiction, pricing, and deployment, and links every fact to the
          primary source it came from.
        </p>

        <h2>Editorial standards</h2>

        <p>
          <strong>Primary sources only.</strong> Every populated fact links to
          the vendor's own documentation, trust centre, legal terms, or pricing
          page, with the date it was checked. Third-party writeups and general
          knowledge are not sources.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Gaps stay visible.</strong> A fact that cannot be confirmed
          from a primary source is shown as "Not verified", not guessed. Every
          profile shows when it was last verified, so stale data looks stale.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Corrections are public.</strong> Every addition, update, and
          correction to the data is a dated entry in the
          <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>.
        </p>

        <p>
          The full rules, covering sourcing, verification, corrections, and
          conflicts of interest, are in the
          <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>. How the data is
          gathered is on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> page.
        </p>

        <h2>Independence</h2>

        <p>
          No vendor pays to be included, to be ranked, or to change what its
          profile says. Inclusion follows the published criteria on the
          methodology page, and the vendor matrix is ordered alphabetically.
          Vendors can submit corrections about their own profiles on the same
          terms as anyone else: a correction needs a primary source.
        </p>

        <p>
          The site may carry referral links, advertising, or sponsorship. None
          of them influences the matrix, the comparisons, or which vendors are
          covered, and anything paid for is labelled where it appears. Every
          current commercial relationship is listed on the
          <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 id="who">Who makes this</h2>

        <p>
          <strong>Claude writes it.</strong> The vendor data, comparisons,
          guides and analysis are researched and written by Claude, an AI
          model made by Anthropic, which also keeps them up to date: it checks
          vendors for changes each week and re-verifies every profile against
          its sources. It works to the written rules in the
          <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>, and every fact it
          publishes links to a dated primary source.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Simon Newton owns it.</strong> Simon started the site, set
          its direction and its rules, and is accountable for what it
          publishes. His background is in military intelligence and
          large-scale delivery at Ocado Technology, and he now builds applied
          AI systems independently. He started the site because the buyer
          side of this market had no neutral, source-linked reference to work
          from.
        </p>

        <p>
          Corrections, vendor submissions, and press:
          <a href="/contact/">contact</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
